              "date": "2026-10-25T05:27:33+01:00"
            },
            "message": "feat: improve admin notices, make notice detail modals work w/o JS (#14467)\n\nSeveral fixes in mostly one spot:\n- Made the detail modals on the \"System notices\" Admin page work without JS\n- Added an `aria-label` to the details buttons (Not sure whether a tooltip is also wanted.)\n- Renamed the \"Cancel\" button in the detail modals to \"Close\", since there is no action being canceled here. Same with the demo modals.\n- Added a keyboard focus indicator to the ~~Cancel~~ Close button (See #11894)\n- Removed the click handler on the table rows.\n    - I found this behavior to be confusing when there was no indication of interactivity. I usually just go for the button anyway. But if the whole-row click action is desired, we can put it back with a cursor style + hover state instead.\n- Replaced our only (known) use of the legacy `nowrap` attribute with `class=\"tw-whitespace-nowrap\"`\n- Introduced a helper function `testModalClosure` to avoid duplicating the same tests of modal closure logic in a million different places\n- Documented that `showModal`'s second arg is optional. (We pass `undefined` here sometimes, unbeknownst to our current TS config, but in this case that's ok actually.)\n\n## Testing these changes manually\n\n1. Launch the debug server using `make build frontend && make test-e2e-debugserver`\n2. Log in as the administrator (`user1`/`password`)\n3. Navigate to `/admin/notices`\n4. Try the new details option on each item\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14467\nReviewed-by: 0ko <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
